## Durable test mission contract

Follow global `worker-test` / `e2e-cockpit` for receipt and question/ACK usage.
FIFO plus tick dispatches work at sequence 0 without heartbeat; run the exact
`accept-dispatch` receipt, start only on `accepted` / `start_work=true`
(sequence 1), then `heartbeat` running sequence 2. Duplicate is not a test rerun.
`ask` / `access-prompt` use private typed body refs; `pending` / `read-question`
return durable mission-status JSON. Only explicit human replies;
`hold --answers` does not approve. Inspect `status.pending_commands` /
`command-status`; accepted-worker cancel/replace requires accepted then applied
ACK with matching digest and typed `--result` after safely stopping. Reuse
IDs/digests, journal no secrets, and keep lifecycle separate from pane diagnosis.
No raw `send`/`nudge` mission, approval or cancel shortcuts.

If the parent repo has `graphify-out/graph.json` and `graphify` is available,
use `graphify query "<question>" --graph "$REPO/graphify-out/graph.json"`
before broad text search for codebase, architecture, file-relationship, and
project-content questions. Include the graph path in fix briefs when useful.

